  "worked_solution": "In this case, the area of the right triangle is\n\n$$\nA=\\frac{1}{2}AC\\cdot BC.\n$$\n\nWe are given that $m\u2220A={45}^{\u2218}.$ Notice that relative to $\u2220A,$ we have expressions for the lengths of the opposite side $\\overset{\u2015}{BC}$ and adjacent side $\\overset{\u2015}{AC}.$ Hence, we can use the tangent ratio to solve for $x:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{tan}\u2061(m\u2220A) & =\\frac{BC}{AC} \\\\ \\operatorname{tan}\u2061({45}^{\u2218}) & =\\frac{5x+5}{6x} \\\\ 1 & =\\frac{5x+5}{6x} \\\\ 6x & =5x+5 \\\\ x & =5\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, the side lengths are\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}AC & =6x=6(5)=30, \\\\ BC & =5x+5=5(5)+5=30.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the area of $\u25b3ABC$ is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}A & =\\frac{1}{2}\\cdot AC\\cdot BC \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}\\cdot 30\\cdot 30 \\\\  & =450.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
